/target
/node_modules
/dist
*.log
.DS_Store
src-tauri/target/
package-lock.json
.winget
certs/
.wibey/
.claude/
videos/

# Tauri regenerates these on every build; they churned in every worktree and PR.
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Seeded design-canvas output — regenerated from the .dc.html working files
design/**/yames-app-redesign.html
design/**/yames-site-directions.html

# Local-only browser preview shim (see src/devShim.local.ts)
src/devShim.local.ts

# Python bytecode from the sound generators in scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Before/after clips of Jam's mix, rendered for the owner's ear. Audio is
# never committed: it is regenerated from `scripts/sounds/jam_mix_probe.ts`
# and `render_band_demos` whenever somebody needs to hear it again.
jam-mix-demos/

# Playwright: the browser it downloads, and what a failing layout run leaves
# behind (screenshots and traces of the moment it failed).
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# W28's A/B clips of a song's band: the recorded half against the synthesised
# one, rendered so the owner can judge by ear. Audio is never committed, for
# the reason `jam-mix-demos` is not — it is rendered again by
# `render_song_ab` whenever somebody needs to hear it.
song-ab-clips/

# The frames a jam clip is painted from (W32), written by
# `tests/layout/jam-clip-frames.spec.ts` so a person — or an agent that
# cannot see the app — can LOOK at what the compositor draws. Rendered
# again by that spec whenever somebody needs to look; never committed.
.jam-frames/

# What the Songs stage looks like at the two windows W34 is argued at, and
# the long fixture scrolled to bar 100, written by
# `tests/layout/songs-stage.spec.ts` and `songs-long.spec.ts`. Pictures of the
# app, for the reason `.jam-shots` exists: a suite can measure a rectangle,
# and only a person (or an agent that can read a PNG) can say whether the tab
# is using the room. Rendered again by those specs; never committed.
.w34-shots/

# What the jam drawer looks like with a take open in it (W33), written by
# `tests/layout/jam-watch.spec.ts` at three widths in two themes. Pictures of
# the app rather than of a canvas, for the same reason `.jam-frames` exists:
# the suite can measure a rectangle, and only a person can say whether the
# thing is worth opening. Rendered again by that spec; never committed.
.jam-shots/

# W31's saved videos and the frames pulled out of them: whether the tablature
# in a clip is readable is a question only a picture answers, so they are
# exported from the shots harness and looked at. Video is never committed, for
# the reason the audio above is not — it is made again whenever the drawing
# changes, and the scripts that make it live beside it.
tab-clips/

# The Songs stage as W36 argues it: the one bar at the top, the strip's air,
# the "More" panel with two parts and with twelve, and three themes' type —
# at 1100, 1440 and 2000×1124, rail open and collapsed. Written by
# `tests/layout/songs-room.spec.ts`, `songs-seek.spec.ts`, `songs-more.spec.ts`
# and `songs-type.spec.ts`. Pictures of the app; never committed.
.w36-shots/

# The songs library, photographed for a person to look at (W35): the shelf
# on its own, three of the player's own songs with the shelf folded under them,
# and a title far wider than the panel — three themes, two languages, two
# widths. Written by `tests/layout/songs-library-shots.spec.ts`; never committed.
.songs-library-shots/
